# verbs.pdl - the teario-play manifest: the known verbs as data (read by the engine's `help` and by `audit`, which checks that every PROJECTION in state.pdl names a verb listed here).
#   VERB | name | page | ui | args | what it does          (the grammar of @.apps/deskopoly/verbs.pdl)
VERB | new       | no | ui | [seed]       | open the game: the first ledger row records the seed, the ruleset name, the rules hash and the kind
VERB | status    | no | ui | -            | read-only: the whole state, derived by replaying the ledger
VERB | replay    | no | ui | -            | read-only: replay the ledger and print its state hash (refuses a ledger that does not reproduce itself)
VERB | check     | no | ui | -            | read-only: replay plus invariants
VERB | ckpt      | no | ui | -            | pin: append a row holding the state hash; every later replay must reproduce it
VERB | ledger_hash | no | ui | [skip_verb] | read-only digest of the ledger rows, optionally without one verb
VERB | audit     | no | ui | -            | read-only no-ghost-data check: the state folder holds only the files state.pdl declares
VERB | ui        | no | ui | -            | write ui.txt: the window feed, a projection of the replayed ledger
VERB | help      | no | ui | -            | list the verbs (from this file)
VERB | join      | no | ui | name [human|pet] | add a player in the lobby (next free id p1..); the roster is a ledger fact
VERB | start     | no | ui | -            | close the lobby (one hero)
VERB | seat      | no | ui | pN human|pet | change who drives a seat (a ledger row, legal at any time)
VERB | input     | no | ui | pN left,right,stay [tick] | steer: ONE ledger row per INPUT (an edge), round = the logical tick; ticks themselves are never rows
VERB | advance   | no | ui | [n]          | simulate n logical ticks (pet seats steer), a ckpt row every ckpt_every ticks and at the end
VERB | tick      | no | ui | -            | ONE logical tick (the driver's step); a ckpt row on every ckpt_every-th tick and when the game ends
VERB | autoplay  | no | ui | -            | tick until the game is over (every seat must be a pet)
VERB | verify_clear | no | ui | -          | read-only: replay the run ledger; if it ends at the goal print `CLEAR level=<hex>;run=<hex>;ticks=<n>` (the proof Make records), else exit 1
VERB | export    | no | ui | out_dir     | read-only: game.csv, events.csv, schema.pdl for the data studio into out_dir
VERB | tuning    | no | ui | -            | read-only: the pace the driver will use, from tuning.pdl tick_ms (33 to 2000 ms per tick at the normal speed); a value outside the range is refused with the reason (exit 2)
